# Copy to .env in this directory. Vite reads its own project root, not the repo root.
# .env is ignored by git: everything personal to your setup lives here.
#
# WARNING: Vite inlines VITE_* into the public client bundle. URLs and flags
# only — never a key, token, or pairing secret.

# --- Packaging your own build (npm run pack) ---------------------------------
# Your own Even Hub package id: reverse-domain, lowercase letters and digits
# only (no hyphens/underscores). It must be yours — the Hub keys builds by it.
# JOAT_PACKAGE_ID=com.yourname.joat
#
# Your Mac(s), as private Tailscale Serve WSS URLs ending in /glasses.
# Comma-separated; the plugin tries them in order. These become the package's
# entire network allowlist.
# JOAT_RELEASE_WS_URLS=wss://your-mac.your-tailnet.ts.net/glasses

# --- Development (npm run dev, simulator) ------------------------------------
# WebSocket target for the Mac brain while developing. MUST match a whitelist
# entry in app.json's network permission — a mismatch fails silently (socket
# never opens, no error). Scheme and port both matter. The checked-in
# app.json allows only ws://127.0.0.1:8787 and ws://localhost:8787 (the
# simulator on the same Mac); add your own origin locally to test from a phone.
# VITE_MAC_WS_URL=ws://127.0.0.1:8787/glasses
